}","target":{"path":"/lessons/03","hash":"#ch-3-2","query":{"tab-2":"code"}}},"122":{"title":"3.2 Colormap: 3 Types","breadcrumb":"Ch 3 · Color","kind":"demo","text":"Sequential / Diverging / Qualitative. Choosing the wrong type = misleading your readers.","target":{"path":"/lessons/03","hash":"#ch-3-2","query":{"tab-2":"demo"}}},"123":{"title":"3.3 CIE Lab Gamut","breadcrumb":"Ch 3 · Color","kind":"explain","text":"What does the gamut look like inside a perceptually uniform color space?","target":{"path":"/lessons/03","hash":"#ch-3-3","query":{"tab-3":"explain"}}},"124":{"title":"3.3 CIE Lab Gamut","breadcrumb":"Ch 3 · Color","kind":"explain","text":"RGB space is a cube, but you cannot tell "which colors actually exist and which would be distorted". CIE Lab is a perceptually uniform space, distance ≈ perceived difference, and is the standard for designing colormaps and checking gamut.","target":{"path":"/lessons/03","hash":"#ch-3-3","query":{"tab-3":"explain"}}},"125":{"title":"3.3 CIE Lab Gamut","breadcrumb":"Ch 3 · Color","kind":"explain","text":"sRGB: universal screen standard (Web / PPT / general scientific figures)
