Use a sequential colormap (e.g., Viridis)—see Chapter 3 §3.2 Colormap","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-3","query":{"tab-3":"explain"}}},"223":{"title":"5.3 Calendar Heatmap (van Wijk)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"explain","text":"Check whether 7 days ago and today are in the same month—if so, draw a same-month separator; otherwise draw a month-divider. This is the core algorithm of calendar visualization.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-3","query":{"tab-3":"explain"}}},"224":{"title":"5.3 Calendar Heatmap (van Wijk)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"code","text":"Display a full year of data with “year = row / week = column”—reveal periodicity + weekly trends + holiday anomalies.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-3","query":{"tab-3":"code"}}},"225":{"title":"5.3 Calendar Heatmap (van Wijk)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"code","text":"Key Point 1: d3.timeDay.range + d3.timeFormat.isoDate
d3.timeDay.range(start, stop) combines “intra-day continuity + structure”—it automatically slices a whole year by day, with leap-year 366 / common-year 365 handled correctly.

Key Point 2: Sunday-first layout
Sunday vs Monday layout is a calendar heatmap design fork: Sunday-first is the English calendar convention (2024-01-01 is Monday, so in its column row 1 is Mon→Sat and the last row is Sun). Chinese settings often switch to Monday-first.

Key Point 3: isMonthDivider month separation
Instead of looping to “find each month’s first day,” use “are 7 days ago and today in the same month?”—simple and correct, just an O(n) single-pass scan. This is the elegant algorithm from calendar heatmap author van Wijk.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-3","query":{"tab-3":"code"}}},"226":{"title":"5.3 Calendar Heatmap (van Wijk)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"code","text":"//  把"年"拆成"日"列表
const days = d3.timeDay.range(
  new Date(2024, 0, 1),         // 2024-01-01
  new Date(2025, 0, 1)          // 2025-01-01
).map(d => ({
  date:  d,
  value: byKey.get(d3.timeFormat('%Y-%m-%d')(d)) ?? 0
}));
// 现在 days.length === 366（2024 闰年）

function weekColSunday(date) {
  // 周日为每列起点 (getDay()=0)
  return Math.floor((d3.timeDay.count(
    d3.timeYear.floor(date), date)) / 7);
}
function dayIndexSunday(date) {
  return date.getDay();    // 0=周日, 1=周一, ..., 6=周六
}

// 渲染每个日格
g.selectAll('rect.cell')
  .data(days).join('rect')
  .attr('class', 'cell')
  .attr('width',  cellSize)
  .attr('height', cellSize)
  .attr('x', d => weekColSunday(d.date) * cellSize)
  .attr('y', d => dayIndexSunday(d.date) * cellSize)
  .attr('rx', 2).attr('ry', 2)
  .attr('fill', d => color(d.value));

//  巧妙算法：判断 7 天前是否同月
function isMonthDivider(date) {
  const sevenDaysAgo = d3.timeDay.offset(date, -7);
  return date.getFullYear() !== sevenDaysAgo.getFullYear()
      || date.getMonth()    !== sevenDaysAgo.getMonth();
}
// 同月：不画分割线；跨月：画一条上边框

function isFirstDayOfMonth(date) {
  return date.getDay() !== 0         // 排除周日（被周列开头替代）
      && date.getMonth() > 0         // 排除一月（画上边框没意义）
      && date.getDate() === 1;
}","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-3","query":{"tab-3":"code"}}},"227":{"title":"5.3 Calendar Heatmap (van Wijk)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"demo","text":"Display a full year of data with “year = row / week = column”—reveal periodicity + weekly trends + holiday anomalies.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-3","query":{"tab-3":"demo"}}},"228":{"title":"5.4 Cyclic Time Viz (Archimedean Spiral)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"explain","text":"Place time along a circle (spiral = circle + continuous unwinding). Reveal periodicity: each loop = one cycle.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-4","query":{"tab-4":"explain"}}},"229":{"title":"5.4 Cyclic Time Viz (Archimedean Spiral)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"explain","text":"Original section 6.2.3 used an Archimedean spiral (uniform-velocity spiral) to lay out dates, with each loop representing 1 year / 1 month / 1 week. Each date corresponds to a sector ring on the spiral.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-4","query":{"tab-4":"explain"}}},"230":{"title":"5.4 Cyclic Time Viz (Archimedean Spiral)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"explain","text":"Spiral vs line: a line captures “trend” in a linear time domain but struggles with “cycle”; a spiral repeats around the circle, highlighting periodicity.
Archimedean Spiral: r = a + bθ, with uniform unwinding (radius increases by a constant b per revolution).
Dynamic Δθ algorithm: the original document’s elegant move—Δθ = boxSize / √(b² + r²), which keeps each sector ring’s arc length roughly equal, preserving visual consistency.
Practical trade-offs: spirals suit “year / season / week” cycles, but are unsuitable when there is “no cycle” or “the cycle is too long”.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-4","query":{"tab-4":"explain"}}},"231":{"title":"5.4 Cyclic Time Viz (Archimedean Spiral)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"explain","text":"Each date maps to a sector ring on the spiral—4 key points: outer start / outer end / inner end / inner start, closing back to the start.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-4","query":{"tab-4":"explain"}}},"232":{"title":"5.4 Cyclic Time Viz (Archimedean Spiral)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"code","text":"Place time along a circle (spiral = circle + continuous unwinding). Reveal periodicity: each loop = one cycle.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-4","query":{"tab-4":"code"}}},"233":{"title":"5.4 Cyclic Time Viz (Archimedean Spiral)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"code","text":"Key Point 1: polar → Cartesian coordinates
Polar = (r, θ), Cartesian = (x, y); θ grows by 2π, r grows by b—this produces a “one ring out per loop” spiral. If b=0, it becomes an ordinary circle.

Key Point 2: dynamic angle increment
This formula is the original document’s core insight: as the radius grows, the same angle spans a longer arc, so Δθ must shrink as r grows—keeping each sector ring’s arc length roughly equal and visually uniform.

Key Point 3: sector-ring path generation
SVG path in essence: M move, L line, Z close. Computing the 4 vertices by hand is more flexible than d3.arc() (which is built for circular arcs and cannot directly handle a spiral).","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-4","query":{"tab-4":"code"}}},"234":{"title":"5.4 Cyclic Time Viz (Archimedean Spiral)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"code","text":"//  阿基米德螺旋公式：r = a + bθ
const boxSize = 32;                  // 每环宽度
const coilGap = boxSize * 1.2;       // 螺旋间距
const b = coilGap / (2 * Math.PI);   // 半径增长系数
const startRadius = 100;
let theta = (startRadius - 0) / b;   // 起始角度

function pos(t) {                    // t: 角度（弧度）
  const r = 0 + b * t;
  return {
    x: r * Math.cos(t),              // 极坐标转笛卡尔
    y: r * Math.sin(t),
    r
  };
}

//  弧长近似相等：Δθ = boxSize / √(b² + r²)
function angleDelta(currentRadius) {
  return boxSize / Math.sqrt(b * b + currentRadius * currentRadius);
}

// 沿螺旋前进 N 天
let t = startTheta;
for (let day = 0; day < 365; day++) {
  const p = pos(t);
  // ...画第 day 天的扇环
  t += angleDelta(p.r);   // 动态加角度
}

//  4 关键点：起点外 → 终点外 → 终点内 → 起点内
function segmentPath(t0, t1) {
  const coords = (t, sign) => {
    const r = pos(t).r + sign * coilGap / 2;  // sign=+1 外圈 / -1 内圈
    return [r * Math.cos(t), r * Math.sin(t)];
  };
  const [x0o, y0o] = coords(t0, +1);
  const [x1o, y1o] = coords(t1, +1);
  const [x1i, y1i] = coords(t1, -1);
  const [x0i, y0i] = coords(t0, -1);
  return `M ${x0o} ${y0o} L ${x1o} ${y1o} L ${x1i} ${y1i} L ${x0i} ${y0i} Z`;
}
// d 属性 = 'M ... L ... L ... L ... Z'，4 个 L 描述一个 4 边形","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-4","query":{"tab-4":"code"}}},"235":{"title":"5.4 Cyclic Time Viz (Archimedean Spiral)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"demo","text":"Place time along a circle (spiral = circle + continuous unwinding). Reveal periodicity: each loop = one cycle.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-4","query":{"tab-4":"demo"}}},"236":{"title":"5.5 Storyline (Jurassic Park)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"explain","text":"Multi-character narrative: each line = one character / organization / process, y-position = togetherness vs apartness, time = story progress.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-5","query":{"tab-5":"explain"}}},"237":{"title":"5.5 Storyline (Jurassic Park)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"explain","text":"Original section 6.2.4 used five characters from Jurassic Park (Alan / T-REX / Raptors / Malcolm / Dilophosaurus) to build a Storyline timeline. The event layer marks key conflicts with semi-transparent red circles.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-5","query":{"tab-5":"explain"}}},"238":{"title":"5.5 Storyline (Jurassic Park)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"explain","text":"Storyline origin: introduced by Ogawa & Ma at Stanford in 2008, originally for movie / academic collaborator networks.
Core idea: abstract each character / organization / process as a “life line,” where lines close = meeting / conflict, lines apart = separation.
Three Key Elements:
Time-scale Mapping: movie duration → SVG width, with the x-axis strictly proportional
Catmull-Rom Spline: curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5) tension coefficient 0.5, “naturally flowing” but not “over-curved”
Event Layer: semi-transparent red circles + text, marking key turning points
Use cases: film analysis, multi-party case timelines, sports interactions, project task handovers.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-5","query":{"tab-5":"explain"}}},"239":{"title":"5.5 Storyline (Jurassic Park)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"explain","text":"monotoneX guarantees “no over-curving” but makes lines “too straight,” losing the narrative “river feel”. Catmull-Rom’s 0.5 tension is an empirical value—flows well without oscillating.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-5","query":{"tab-5":"explain"}}},"240":{"title":"5.5 Storyline (Jurassic Park)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"code","text":"Multi-character narrative: each line = one character / organization / process, y-position = togetherness vs apartness, time = story progress.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-5","query":{"tab-5":"code"}}},"241":{"title":"5.5 Storyline (Jurassic Park)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"code","text":"Key Point 1: each character = one path
Using y to encode “relationships” is the key: T-REX and Grant both at y=130 at t=78, so the two lines visually converge = “T-REX attacks Grant.” This isn’t algorithmically generated—it’s manual narrative design, but d3 gives you the tools to do it by hand.

Key Point 2: event layer (narrative anchors)
Decouple event layer from line layer: the line layer expresses “relationship flow,” the event layer expresses “narrative anchors.” This two-layer structure is the standard Storyline design—each can be animated or filtered independently.

Key Point 3: alpha(0.5) tension coefficient
0.5 is an empirical value: softer than 0 (looks narrative), steadier than 1.0 (no roller-coaster). Use 0.5 for time-based narratives; use 0.2–0.3 for scientific curve fitting (closer to data).","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-5","query":{"tab-5":"code"}}},"242":{"title":"5.5 Storyline (Jurassic Park)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"code","text":"//  时间尺度：0-127 分钟 → 屏幕宽度
const xScale = d3.scaleLinear()
  .domain([0, 127])
  .range([50, width - 50]);

// 每个角色是一组 [time, y] 关键点（手工调 y 实现聚散）
const characters = [
  { name: 'T-REX', color: '#d32f2f', points: [
    {time: 75, y: 280}, {time: 78, y: 130},   // 攻击现场
    {time: 88, y: 200}, {time:120, y: 290}
  ]},
  { name: 'Grant', color: '#1976d2', points: [
    {time:  0, y: 100}, {time: 78, y: 130},   // 与 T-REX 聚拢
    {time:120, y:  50}
  ]}
];

// 路径生成器
const line = d3.line()
  .curve(d3.curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5))   // 张力 0.5
  .x(d => xScale(d.time))
  .y(d => d.y);

characters.forEach(c => {
  svg.append('path')
    .datum(c.points)
    .attr('d', line)
    .attr('stroke', c.color)
    .attr('stroke-width', 3)
    .attr('fill', 'none');
});

//  事件层：半透明红圈 + 文字标签
const events = [
  { time: 78, x: xScale(78), y: 130, name: 'T-REX 攻击',
    desc: 'T-REX 冲出围栏攻击 Alan & Kids 的车' },
  { time: 48, x: xScale(48), y: 320, name: 'Nedry 事件',
    desc: 'Dilophosaurus 攻击 Nedry' }
];

const eventLayer = svg.append('g').attr('class', 'event-layer');

eventLayer.selectAll('g.event')
  .data(events).enter().append('g')
  .attr('class', 'event')
  .style('cursor', 'pointer')
  .on('mouseenter', (e, d) => showTip(`${d.name}\n${d.desc}`))
  .each(function (d) {
    // 半透明背景圈
    d3.select(this).append('circle')
      .attr('cx', d.x).attr('cy', d.y).attr('r', 20)
      .attr('fill', 'rgba(255,0,0,0.15)');
    // 文字
    d3.select(this).append('text')
      .attr('x', d.x).attr('y', d.y - 9)
      .attr('text-anchor', 'middle')
      .attr('font-size', 10).attr('font-weight', 600)
      .attr('fill', '#cc0000')
      .text(d.name);
  });

// d3.curveCatmullRom.alpha(t) - t ∈ [0, 1]
// t=0: 接近 linear（接近直线）
// t=0.5: 标准 Catmull-Rom（推荐）
// t=1.0: 接近 cardinal（高度曲线化）
d3.line().curve(d3.curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5));","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-5","query":{"tab-5":"code"}}},"243":{"title":"5.5 Storyline (Jurassic Park)","breadcrumb":"Ch 5 · Time Series","kind":"demo","text":"Multi-character narrative: each line = one character / organization / process, y-position = togetherness vs apartness, time = story progress.","target":{"path":"/lessons/05","hash":"#ch-5-5","query":{"tab-5":"demo"}}},"244":{"title":"Demo 1 · D3 数据加载器","breadcrumb":"Ch 1 · Data","kind":"standalone","text":"对应讲义章节 3.5 D3 数据选择器。本 demo 演示 异步加载 CSV、字段名映射（中文 → 英文）和 类型转换（字符串 → Number / Date）的完整流程。
